From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:46:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: Remove conflicting framebuffers

On phones the bootloader leaves the panel scanning out a framebuffer that
simpledrm or simplefb drives until a display driver takes over.
mediatek-drm never removed them, so after it bound both drivers kept
their devices and the firmware framebuffer stayed the system's first
DRM device and fbdev. Remove conflicting framebuffer devices before
registering, as rockchip and sun4i do.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
index fcfb0d43..92891edb 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  * Author: YT SHEN <yt.shen@mediatek.com>
  */
 
+#include <linux/aperture.h>
 #include <linux/component.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
@@ -668,6 +669,11 @@ static int mtk_drm_bind(struct device *dev)
 	if (!mtk_drm_get_all_drm_priv(dev))
 		return 0;
 
+	/* Take the display from a firmware framebuffer driver. */
+	ret = aperture_remove_all_conflicting_devices(mtk_drm_driver.name);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_put_dev;
+
 	drm = drm_dev_alloc(&mtk_drm_driver, dev);
 	if (IS_ERR(drm)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(drm);
